      "message": "feat(model): a linked model is imported again when its source file changes\n\nAn imported model records the file it was read from and that file's\nSHA-256 (schema::ModelSource). The record rides ImportModel, UpdateModel\n(undo restores it; a repair keeps it), DeleteEntity and ImportFixture,\nand the project file keeps it (v68: an optional `source` on a model row;\na v67 file opens unlinked; a malformed row is corrupt).\n\nWhile the project is open in the window, each linked file is checked\nabout once a second (size and time first, then the digest). A new digest\nimports the file again through CommandKind::ImportFile, and it lands on\nthe linked model by name: one UpdateModel, one undo step, the operations\ngo Stale. Nothing regenerates or posts. An undo of that import stays\nuntil the file changes again. A missing file keeps the model and is said\none time. The Browser's model menu has \"Unlink from <file>\"; the MCP tool\nset_model_link links and unlinks, and get_job shows models[].source.\n\nFixes #2463\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MLU9aif5zm7mure23AKftd",
